+# Every name here was checked against RobloxStudioBeta.exe of 0.745.0.7451137: a registered fast variable
+# leaves its name in the binary as a NUL-terminated string without the type prefix, so b'<Name>\x00' must
+# appear. Seven names that used to be in this list do not appear at all and were removed, because Studio
+# ignores a setting it has no variable for:
+#   FFlagDisablePostFx, FIntRenderShadowIntensity, DFFlagDebugRenderForceTechnologyVoxel,
+#   DFFlagTextureQualityOverrideEnabled, DFIntTextureQualityOverride, FIntRenderGrassDetailStrands,
+#   FFlagGlobalWindRendering
+# Two of those mattered: the lighting was never forced to voxel (the cheapest technology), and textures were
+# never pinned to the lowest quality. No replacement flag for either is in the binary -- Lighting.Technology
+# is a property of a place now, not a fast variable. Candidates the binary does have, whose type prefix cannot
+# be confirmed (Roblox pushes no value for them on any clientsettings endpoint, so the prefix would be a
+# guess, and a wrong prefix is silently ignored): RenderForceVideoMemorySize,
+# PerformanceControlLowPowerTextureQualityEnabled/Percent, RenderShadowResolutionScaling,
+# RenderPostFxBasePixelCount. Worth trying one at a time on a device, not worth guessing into the default.
+LIGHT_FLAGS={'DFIntTaskSchedulerTargetFps':24,'DFIntDebugFRMQualityLevelOverride':1,
  # Wine handles Alt+Enter itself; Studio's own handling breaks the window under Wine (as Vinegar sets it).
  'FFlagHandleAltEnterFullscreenManually':False,
